# 30. Definition of Functional Completion

The product is functionally complete when every module behaves according to specification, every user interaction produces predictable and accessible outcomes, all conversion paths operate correctly, and the website delivers a seamless, premium experience across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices while remaining extensible for future business growth.
